Written `ADR-001-notification-architecture.md`. The recommendation is **Redis Streams** with application-level idempotency keys for billing exactly-once delivery. The justification rests on three converging constraints from the system context: the team has no Kafka experience and no dedicated infra engineer, the 2-week delivery window rules out standing up a new distributed system, and we already run Redis in production — so Streams gives us consumer groups, persistent messages, retry via XPENDING/XCLAIM, and dead-letter processing with zero new infrastructure. Kafka is the stronger technical choice at scale, but the operational and budgetary tax makes it the wrong choice for this team at this size right now.
